+### Dielectric Shading
+A shading model for dielectric materials that handles transparency and absorption using stochastic ray selection and Beer-Lambert law [S2, unofficial]. It performs stochastic selection between reflection and refraction rays, and applies Beer-Lambert absorption to the transmitted ray intensity based on distance and absorption density [S2, unofficial].
